# The import fixtures are hashed byte for byte by
# tests/Rag.Companion.Tests/ImportFixtureManifestTests, which compares the manifest's SHA-256 against the bytes
# on disk. With core.autocrlf=true and no -text rule here, a Windows checkout rewrites the line endings of the
# text fixtures - and of sample.pdf, which git also classified as text - so every manifest hash mismatched and the
# companion-windows CI job failed three assertions. -text keeps the committed bytes intact on every platform,
# which is what a hashed fixture requires. The earlier `sample.pdf -whitespace` rule only silenced whitespace
# warnings and did not stop the conversion.
tests/fixtures/import/* -text
